# Build context hygiene for both image builds (context is the repo root).
# Keep this conservative: the agent build needs pyproject.toml, uv.lock, src/,
# README.md and LICENSE; the frontend build needs webapp/frontend/ MINUS its
# local node_modules/.next (which are macOS/arm and must be rebuilt in-image).

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Node — rebuilt inside the image, never ship the host's macOS/arm artifacts
**/node_modules
**/.next

# Python caches / virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
.venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Local env files and secrets — never bake into an image
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
*.env

# Build / test artifacts not needed at build time.
# The generated per-env reports (eval/reports/<env>/) are host state, never baked —
# but the COMMITTED seed archive (eval/reports/seed/) is the floor the eval-driven
# dashboards fall back to when a deployment has no archive of its own (Cloud Run),
# so it MUST ship in the image. Excluding it here is exactly what left the container
# with an empty eval/reports/ and degraded agent_historique to `available: false`.
eval/reports/*
!eval/reports/seed
!eval/reports/seed/**
**/coverage
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.DS_Store
